{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Which YHWH your Elohim seeks.</b> But does He not seek all lands — as it is said, ״לְהַמְטִיר עַל אֶרֶץ לֹא אִישׁ״ (Job 38)? Rather, as it were, He seeks none but it; and through that seeking with which He seeks it, He seeks all the lands along with it." "<b>The eyes of YHWH your Elohim are continually upon it.</b> To see what it needs, and to issue new decrees upon it — times for good, times for bad, etc. — as is found in Rosh Hashanah (17a)." "<b>From the beginning of the year.</b> From the head of the year it is judged what will be at its end (there, 8a)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "Rashi cites the Talmud tractate by its page (דף י\"ז), here resolved as 17a in the standard Vilna pagination of Rosh Hashanah.", 2 "The reference 'שם ח' (there 8) points to page 8 of the same tractate, Rosh Hashanah, resolved as 8a."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:33.180802984Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}